VALUES
  ('capa-001', 'fnd-001', 'PSV-4102 on Crude Column Overhead Accumulator exceeded 36-month certification interval by 120 days.',
   'Immediately performed online ultrasonic wall thickness testing on vessel nozzle; expedited emergency warehouse delivery of identical certified spare valve PSV-4102-SP and completed replacement under hot-standby protocol on 2026-02-14.',
   '5 Why',
   '1. Why was valve overdue? -> Spare was not available in warehouse during scheduled turnaround. 2. Why was spare not available? -> Procurement PO was delayed by 6 weeks. 3. Why was PO delayed? -> SAP reorder point was set to manual instead of auto-replenish. 4. Why manual? -> System migration in 2024 left 42 relief valve parts without min-max thresholds. 5. Root Cause: Lack of automated ERP maintenance trigger and safety device inventory governance.',
   '["1. Why was PSV-4102 overdue? Spare valve was not in warehouse stock during outage.", "2. Why was spare not in stock? Purchase requisition was delayed by 6 weeks at buyer queue.", "3. Why delayed at buyer queue? SAP reorder point was set to manual instead of auto-replenishment.", "4. Why was it set to manual? ERP system master data migration omitted critical spare min-max triggers.", "5. Root Cause: Inadequate PSM critical equipment inventory governance and absence of automated escalation for overdue safety valves."]',
   '{"manpower":["Scheduler relied on manual spreadsheets","Buyer lacked criticality training"],"machine":["No ERP auto-escalation alert when PSV within 90 days of expiry"],"method":["PSV recertification procedure lacked executive escalation protocol"],"material":["Long lead-time Monel trim valve body required 14 weeks from forge"],"measurement":["Inspection backlog was only reviewed quarterly instead of bi-weekly"],"environment":["Turnaround workload compressed maintenance coordination window"]}',
   '1. Install certified replacement PSV-4102 with full API 520 bench test certificate (Done). 2. Audit all 480 refinery PSVs in SAP and establish mandatory auto-reorder thresholds with 90-day lead-time buffers. 3. Configure automated bi-weekly email escalation to Plant Manager for any safety critical equipment within 60 days of expiry. 4. Update refinery PSM Procedure SOP-MI-04 to mandate written GM concession before exceeding any relief device interval.',
   'Auditor C', '2026-03-10', '$14,500 for replacement valve, ERP consultant configuration for SAP PM alert module.', '2026-03-08', 'Work Order #49021 closed out; Bench test certificate #BT-2026-081 attached; SAP auto-escalation screenshot verified.',
   'Implemented & Validated', 'Robert Hayes (Operations Supervisor)', '2026-03-08', 'Verified physical installation of replacement valve body PSV-4102 stamped 75.0 psig with bench test certificate #BT-2026-081 and Work Order #49021 closure.',
   'Pending', 'Auditor B (Lead Auditor)', '2026-05-08', '60-day observation window active: DCS continuous pressure trend confirms nominal 4.2 bar operation, zero relief events, SAP auto-escalation active.', 60,
   '[{"id":"prc-1","code":"SOP-MI-04","title":"Pressure Relief Device Testing & Re-certification Protocol","currentRevision":"Rev 3.2","revisionRequired":true,"targetRevision":"Rev 4.0","status":"In Revision","owner":"Mechanical Integrity Lead"},{"id":"prc-2","code":"WI-SAP-PM-12","title":"Safety-Critical Min-Max Reorder Trigger Protocol","currentRevision":"Rev 1.4","revisionRequired":true,"targetRevision":"Rev 2.0","status":"Needs Revision","owner":"Maintenance Planning"}]',
   '[{"id":"rsk-1","riskCode":"RSK-PSM-018","riskTitle":"Catastrophic Overpressure & Vapor Release at CDU Overhead Accumulator V-401","category":"Operational","preLikelihood":4,"preConsequence":5,"preRiskScore":20,"residualLikelihood":1,"residualConsequence":4,"residualRiskScore":4,"riskRegisterUpdated":true,"reviewedBy":"Process Safety Director"}]',
   '[{"id":"cmp-1","targetRoleOrPerson":"Maintenance Schedulers & Turnaround Planners","requiredCompetency":"API 576 & PSM Critical Relief Device Scheduling Protocol","gapIdentified":"Did not recognize manual PO queue stall for Class-1 relief valves","reTrainingRequired":true,"trainingDueDate":"2026-03-25","completionDate":null,"signoffStatus":"Scheduled","trainerOrVerifier":"Training Superintendent"}]',
   '{"exposureCategory":"Fire & Explosion Hazard","financialExposureBracket":"Catastrophic (>$1M)","businessInterruptionRiskDays":45,"underwriterWarrantyImpact":true,"lossControlRecommendation":"Ensure 100% of API 520 safety relief valves on Class 1 hydrocarbon vessels are monitored with real-time ERP countdown telemetry and redundant certified spares in warehouse.","underwritingAuditStatus":"Mitigation Verified"}',
   'Verified physical installation of valve PSV-4102 with tag #CERT-2026-09. Verified SAP alert configuration trigger tested successfully for next scheduled batches.', 'Auditor B', '2026-03-18', 'Pending Review', 'Under Verification'),
  ('capa-002', 'fnd-002', 'Secondary containment bund drain valve V-219 at Solvent Tank Farm B was left in open, unlocked position.',
   'Valve V-219 was immediately turned to closed position, verified tight, and padlocked with tamper-evident seal #SEAL-9014 at 10:25 AM on 2026-03-13.',
   'Fishbone',
   'Root cause analysis identified absence of standardized checklist at bund gate, lack of visual status flag on high bund walls, and operator haste following heavy rainfall stormwater clearance.',
   '["Why was valve open? Operator opened it to drain rain and failed to close.", "Why failed to close? Operator was called away to urgent pump vibration alarm.", "Why no reminder? No physical tag or control room indicator exists for bund valves.", "Why no visual flag? Bund wall is 2 meters high blocking line of sight from road.", "Root Cause: Administrative procedure relied on human memory without physical barrier or checklist interlock."]',
   '{"manpower":["Single operator handling multiple rain drainage points across 4 tank farms"],"machine":["No limit switch or remote DCS position indication on containment valves"],"method":["Drainage procedure lacked formal pre-drain and post-drain sign-off log at gate"],"material":["Weathered padlock was difficult to clasp quickly"],"measurement":["Stormwater turbidity is logged but valve open/close time was not tracked"],"environment":["Heavy rainstorm caused simultaneous standing water across entire facility"]}',
   '1. Install spring-loaded deadman drain valves or high-visibility red/green physical position indicator flags visible from roadway. 2. Implement weather-resistant lockbox at bund entrance requiring control room key signout for drain valve key. 3. Update SOP-ENV-12 to mandate dual-person verification for secondary containment draining.',
   'Mark Donaldson', '2026-03-27', 'Estimated $3,200 for indicator flags and lockboxes across 6 tank farms.', NULL, 'Emergency closed photo verified; draft procedure SOP-ENV-12 under review.',
   'Pending', NULL, NULL, NULL,
   'Pending', NULL, NULL, NULL, 30,
   '[{"id":"prc-3","code":"SOP-ENV-12","title":"Stormwater Drainage and Containment Bund Isolation Protocol","currentRevision":"Rev 2.0","revisionRequired":true,"targetRevision":"Rev 3.0","status":"Needs Revision","owner":"Environmental Manager"}]',
   '[{"id":"rsk-2","riskCode":"RSK-ENV-009","riskTitle":"Major Loss of Secondary Containment - Aromatic Solvents Release to Ship Channel","category":"Environmental","preLikelihood":4,"preConsequence":4,"preRiskScore":16,"residualLikelihood":2,"residualConsequence":3,"residualRiskScore":6,"riskRegisterUpdated":false,"reviewedBy":"Environmental Compliance Officer"}]',
   '[{"id":"cmp-2","targetRoleOrPerson":"Tank Farm B Field Operators (Shift A-D)","requiredCompetency":"Secondary Containment Drain Lockout & Dual-Signoff Protocol","gapIdentified":"Left valve unclasped following heavy storm without physical tag verification","reTrainingRequired":true,"trainingDueDate":"2026-03-20","completionDate":null,"signoffStatus":"Required","trainerOrVerifier":"Operations Shift Lead"}]',
   '{"exposureCategory":"Environmental Impairment","financialExposureBracket":"Severe ($250k-$1M)","businessInterruptionRiskDays":14,"underwriterWarrantyImpact":true,"lossControlRecommendation":"Install spring-return deadman drain valves or mechanical interlocks preventing gate egress while bund valve is open.","underwritingAuditStatus":"Open Risk Item"}',
   NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Pending Review', 'Draft'),
  ('capa-005', 'fnd-005', 'Missing torque documentation on Heat Exchanger E-104.',
   'Contractor supervisor provided electronic calibration cert for hydraulic torque wrench #HW-402 and signed affidavit confirming 450 ft-lbs torque applied.',
   '5 Why',
   'Subcontractor administrative clerk failed to compile final QA package before leaving site.', NULL, NULL,
   'Mandated that all contractor payment releases require signed QA dossier verification by Lead Inspector.',
   'Robert Hayes', '2025-11-20', 'Administrative only', '2025-11-18', 'Signed torque report #TRQ-2025-09 and calibration sheet for wrench #HW-402.',
   'Implemented & Validated', 'Robert Hayes (Quality Lead)', '2025-11-18', 'Verified calibration certificate for hydraulic torque wrench #HW-402 and 100% torque pack verification form.',
   'Verified Effective (Sustained)', 'Auditor A (Lead Auditor)', '2025-12-05', 'Follow-up inspection during subsequent December turnaround validated 100% compliance with zero torque documentation defects.', 30,
   '[{"id":"prc-4","code":"SOP-QA-08","title":"Heat Exchanger Bolt Torqueing & Gasket Verification","currentRevision":"Rev 4.0","revisionRequired":false,"targetRevision":null,"status":"Approved","owner":"QA Inspection Lead"}]',
   '[{"id":"rsk-3","riskCode":"RSK-MEC-022","riskTitle":"Flange Leakage and Fire Hazard at High-Temp Exchanger Train","category":"Operational","preLikelihood":3,"preConsequence":4,"preRiskScore":12,"residualLikelihood":1,"residualConsequence":2,"residualRiskScore":2,"riskRegisterUpdated":true,"reviewedBy":"Mechanical Integrity Lead"}]',
   '[{"id":"cmp-3","targetRoleOrPerson":"Mechanical Turnaround Sub-Contractors","requiredCompetency":"Documented Hydraulic Torque Wrenches & Digital Calibration Records","gapIdentified":"Missing hand-off verification packet","reTrainingRequired":true,"trainingDueDate":"2025-11-15","completionDate":"2025-11-15","signoffStatus":"Verified","trainerOrVerifier":"Lead Auditor A"}]',
   '{"exposureCategory":"Asset Physical Damage","financialExposureBracket":"Moderate ($50k-$250k)","businessInterruptionRiskDays":5,"underwriterWarrantyImpact":false,"lossControlRecommendation":"Implement mandatory gate signoff holding contractor final invoice release pending QA torque dossier audit.","underwritingAuditStatus":"Endorsed by Surveyor"}',
   'Reviewed next turnaround job in Dec 2025; all torque dossiers were submitted within 24 hours of bolt-up.', 'Auditor A', '2025-12-05', 'Effective - Close Finding', 'Verified Effective');

